From f0a2bef163a667207562e6dbaded9d8dca75b3da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozgur Guzeldereli <ozgur@guzeldereli.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:29:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] TTF decode speed: TQ1_P table-decode matvec, fused TTF
 linear (prologue + matvec with scale, bias, adapter epilogue), K-padded TQ1_P
 weights

- mmvq-tq1p.cuh: TQ1_P matvec for 1-4 tokens decoding trits through a 256-entry shared table; the activation sum
  enters the dp4a accumulator, so each q8_1 block's integer sum is exact
- fused TTF linear for TQ1_P weights: [PAD] MUL(c) ADD(m) MUL_MAT MUL(r) [ADD(b)] [MUL_MAT(D) MUL_MAT(U) ADD] in two
  kernels (prologue: centring + q8_1 quantization + adapter down product, finalized by the last block in a fixed
  order; matvec with row scale, bias and adapter up product in the epilogue)
- loader accepts TQ1_P weights whose K is rounded up to a multiple of 160; build_lora_mm zero-pads the input
- the adapter that reads the main weight's centred input shares it (computed once)
- MUL_MAT + row scale + bias fused into the generic MMVQ epilogue; c * x + m in one kernel
